•	The userdel command deletes a user from the system, with an optional -r flag to also remove the user's home directory and files, though deactivating an account with usermod -L is often a safer alternative.
File Ownership Management
•	The chown command enables changes to the ownership of files and directories, allowing you to specify both the user and group owner of a particular file or directory. 
•	When changing group ownership with chown, a colon (:) must precede the group name to differentiate it from a username.


